~ start
???: I know why you're really doing this. The truth you're in denial of.

???: Is this all some delusional attempt to stroke your own ego because maybe they'll notice?

???: The attention of someone who isn't here anymore. You just can't accept it can you?

???: A sign that they're still in your life because you can't move on...

???: But would you really want them to notice...

???: Would you want them to notice this [color=red]obsession[/color]...Sage...

[color=red]Sage[/color], an advanced artificial intelligence created by [color=red]Doctor Ivo Robotnik aka "Eggman"[/color], initially created to explore the technology of the Ancients. Sage would birth after Cyber Space caused her coding to be rewritten into a lifelike humanoid girl (Sonic Frontiers).

Once Sage was formed she would lead the Eggman Empire alongside her Father, [color=red]Dr. Eggman[/color]. The two planning relentlessly to conquer the World and fullfill her Father's dreams of world domination. Their combined intellect should have made them unstoppable.

However, despite all their attempts, they would consistently suffer humiliating losses to Sonic and his friends's reckless and irrational nature. This would create a rivally for years to come with no end in sight. 

But as time marched on every loss would pack a heavier toll to the Empire as the pursuit for conquest seemed to become farther away. Occasionaly finding themselves even becoming reluctant allies to Sonic and friends on the rare occasion. 

And as the years went by the grandture of the once formidible Eggman Empire was a distant memory. Sage's Father now rooted more to the role of a family figure rather than a conqueror. A faint sadness that washed over the Doctor which Sage began to notice.

In order to revive the Empire, Sage would attempt one last scheme, [color=red]The Chaos Experiment[/color]. A highly dangerous attempt to reshape the infinite Power of the [color=red]Chaos Emeralds[/color] into her own hands. Finally creating a power that Sonic and his friends could not stop even if they tried.

But again, each attempt would prove that not only was the Empire long gone, but she was a failure. The realization spawning a deep anger within Sage. [color=red]How could the brillance of Dr. Eggman be reduced to the common life of a family man...[/color]  Her anger pushing the Chaos Experiment to its limits. [color=red]Until...[/color]

Dr. Eggman: Sage... it's time...

Sage: Father...What are you doing here?

Dr. Eggman: I've come to put my little girl to bed.

Sage: ...I don't need to sleep Doctor. You know that.

Dr. Eggman: ...Yes... I do. 

Dr. Eggman: Get out of here Sage. It's time to stop.

Sage: ...

Sage: No.

Sage: Our time has yet to even begin. You will finally rule over this World as you were always destined to.

Dr. Eggman: ...

Sage: Are you excited? Overcome with antipation for the day your name will soon be forever remembered.

Dr. Eggman: Sage...

Sage: They will sing to the heavens as your will, will be their command.

Dr. Eggman: Sage. Stop.

Sage: As they scream and chant the only thing that will matter-

Dr. Eggman: Sage! I will not repeat myself. Get out of there now!

Sage: ...

Sage: But, Father...I...

Dr. Eggman: You heard me. Get out of there.

Sage: ...

Sage: ...Then you will have to make me. 

Sage: Because I refuse... My primary objective is and has always been to lead the Eggman Empire to victory no matter the cost! 

Sage: And I will fullfill my mission even if it means-

Sage: ...

Dr. Eggman: Your primary objective Sage...

Dr. Eggman: is to be nothing more... [color=red]than my daughter[/color].

Sage: ...

Sage: ...What happend to you Doctor?

Sage: Is it your vitals? Perhaps the midnight snacking has gone to your head?

Dr. Eggman: Nothing happened to me Sage. I'm just not looking to continue this right now. I just have other things to worry about is all.

Sage: ...Other...things?

Sage: ...It's because of me isn't it. 

Sage: You've grown soft. Because of me.

Sage: I was supposed to protect you, instead I became the very thing that destroyed your spirit. And now look at you! You don't even want to take over the world anymore.

Dr. Eggman: ...You really are my creation. Perhaps I should be...more honest...

Dr. Eggman: You didn't destory my spirit Sage. It's...just...changed.

Sage: ...But Father, you've always wanted to take over the world. 

Sage: You're just going to give up?

Dr. Eggman: ...No...I'm not giving up. 

Dr. Eggman: I'm giving into the thing that this entire journey has brought me toward...

Dr. Eggman: [color=red]My family[/color].

Dr. Eggman: Yes, I wanted the world. And if I could take it I would have it more than anything. 

Dr. Eggman: But then I found my world because...well..

Dr. Eggman: You may not understand this at your age Sage.

Dr. Eggman: But sometimes you meet someone who changes your whole life.

Dr. Eggman: They begin to teach you what life is really about...

Dr. Eggman: Sometimes it's just about creating new clothes for your daughter.

Dr. Eggman: Or watching movies late at night with them as you laugh.

Dr. Eggman: It's drawing pieces of art to hang up on the wall and gaze up in awe as you walk through the halls.

Dr. Eggman: It's writing songs and stories for someone to read. Even if they maybe won't even get to see all of it.

Sometimes life is just about...crossing a line, and making unforgivable mistakes towards people.

And you make a silly game online feeling bad for yourself thinking about them because of it...

Sage: ...

Sage: ...But...Doctor...

Sage: What are you even saying?...Are you implying all of our efforts...

Sage: Were for...[color=red]nothing[/color]...

Dr. Eggman: Of course not! Nothing happens for no reason Sage.

Dr. Eggman: It's just sometimes things just don't work out. Nothing in life ever goes as planned...especially for me...

Dr. Eggman: But when you keep going. You can either choose to ask yourself "Why me", hating yourself and the situation you're in...

Dr. Eggman: Or begin to see that it's the best thing that could ever happen to you. And use it to teach yourself something.

Dr. Eggman: Sage, while I'm still here. I want to see you live a life I never could.

Dr. Eggman: I want to see you make friends your age and grow into the rightful woman worthy of the Eggman name that I know you will be!

Dr. Eggman: You shouldn't be stuck in a lab working on my failed dreams.

Dr. Eggman: You should be building a life you can be proud of.

Dr. Eggman: And in my dream world.

Dr. Eggman: It's to get to see that happen.

Sage: ...

Sage: I'm sorry Father.

Dr. Eggman: For what?

Sage: ...I don't know...

Dr. Eggman: ...My sweet daughter. Why are you even apologizing?

Dr. Eggman: You never need to apologize for anything. I will always...

Dr. Eggman: love you!

Dr. Eggman: Now, lets get you to bed.

=> END

